          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em quark-gluon plasma
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+of+matter"} phase of matter
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            at extremely high
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temperature"} temperature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            are not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            but propagate freely together with the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plasma"} plasma
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+of+matter"} phase
            where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/protons"} protons
            are no longer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atoms"} atoms
            but propagate freely, one speaks of
            = succeed "." do
              %em quark-gluon plasma
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/QCDPhaseDiagram.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              %strong
                Schematic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+diagram"} phase diagram
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              The vertical axis indicates
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temperature"} temperature
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density"} density
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
              only appear as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"}> confinement
              ). But above a critical temperature these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
              break apart (deconfinement) and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
              may exist freely. This
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+of+matter"} phase
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %em quark-gluon plasma
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Blaizot03"} Blaizot 03
          %h3#nonperturbative_regime Non-perturbative regime
          %p
            Despite the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} deconfinement
            beyond
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temperature"} temperature
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                  %mn 4
                  %mo −
                  %mn 5
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim 4-5 T_c
            as produced in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            (
            %a{:href => "#AdamsEtAl05"}> Adams et al. 05
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AdcoxEtAl05"} Adcox et al. 05
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupled
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
            requiring discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+field+theory"} non-perturbative field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
            computer simulation. Indication for strong coupling of the QG-plasma comes from the nature of the
            %em elliptic flow
            seen both in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            as well as in these computer simulations, which shows
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hydrodynamic"} hydrodynamic
            behaviour with extremely small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shear+viscosity"} shear viscosity
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Shuryak01"} Shuryak 01
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Chakraborty12"} Chakraborty 12
          %p
            It has been proposed (
            %a{:href => "#PolicastroSonStarinets01"}> Policastro-Son-Starinets 01
            ) that, therefore, an analytic approach to a description of the quark-gluon plasma (i.e. not just via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
            computer experiment) might be given by approximate
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+duality"} AdS-CFT duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD+correspondence"} AdS/QCD correspondence
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fluid%2Fgravity+correspondence"} fluid/gravity correspondence
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BiagazziCotrone12"} Biagazzi-Cotrone 12
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            (as opposed to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D4+D%3D4+SYM"} N=4 D=4 SYM
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+duality"} AdS-CFT duality
            applies only to some approximation, see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD+correspondence"} AdS/QCD correspondence
            for more.
          %h3#perturbative_regime Perturbative regime
          %p
            At yet higher energies, the quark-gluon plasma is eventually supposed to be weakly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupled
            again, due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+freedom"} asymptotic freedom
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Blaizot03"} Blaizot 03
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#EarlyCosmologyAndNucleosynthesis Early cosmology and nucleosynthesis
          %p
            In the
